+Function arguments use `response.function_call_arguments.delta` and `.done`. For ordinary,
+non-strict Qwen tools without grammar constraints, streaming Responses preview recognizable
+parameters of the first tool call as decoding progresses. The preview escapes recognized values
+as JSON strings, so it can show temporary string types or repeated fields. The existing terminal
+parser remains authoritative: `response.function_call_arguments.done.arguments`,
+`response.output_item.done.item.arguments`, and the terminal Response contain the same normalized
+arguments. A client must use the finished item, not the preview, to execute a tool. IDs and output
+indices are stable across the events; an unmatched provisional item is not completed as a tool call.
+
+The preview is enabled by default for streaming Responses requests. Set `kvmem_tool_preview: false`
+in the request body for terminal-only tool arguments (whose concatenated deltas equal the final
+arguments). Later tool calls and other tool syntaxes retain terminal-only behavior. Responses SSE
+has no Chat Completions `[DONE]` sentinel. Ordinary answer text still streams immediately; tool
+markup that never opens a function is returned as ordinary text by the existing decoder.
 
